From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:45:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock native Chrome navigation timing entries

Expose a Window-only PerformanceNavigationTiming interface inheriting
PerformanceResourceTiming and PerformanceEntry. Lazily allocate one native
navigation entry per document and reuse existing timeline getters, ordering,
identity and buffered PerformanceObserver delivery.

Mock type as navigate (including reload/history traversals), status as 200,
HTML content type, zero timings/sizes/redirectCount, empty protocol/encoding
and null notRestoredReasons. Include inherited and navigation fields in
native toJSON. Do not add network timing collection, lifecycle measurement,
new polling tasks, per-resource work or JavaScript shims.

Retain a page-owned document-navigation URL separately from mutable SPA URLs
and from the owning context, so a saved iframe Performance remains safe and
keeps its original name after context teardown. Workers do not gain navigation
entries or the constructor.

Fashion Nova's root bundle directly evaluates instanceof
PerformanceNavigationTiming in an affiliate effect. Its missing interface
throws a ReferenceError and renders the React error boundary; supplying only
the missing constructor restored the cart contract in diagnostics. This patch
returns the lightweight Chromium-like native shape instead of a page shim.
Reference: https://w3c.github.io/navigation-timing/

Adjust existing upstream resource-order/buffer and supported-entry-type
expectations for the added navigation entry. Add no upstream unit tests.
